# The memql commit every CI lane checks out as the ../memql sibling.
#
# This file is the SINGLE source of truth for that pin. Workflows must not
# name a ref themselves -- they reach the sibling through
# .github/actions/checkout-memql, which reads this file. The guard job in
# ci.yml fails if any workflow checks out znasllc-io/memql directly.
#
# WHY PINNED. memql is being split into ~29 nested modules (memql#3228). No
# static cockpit go.mod is green both before and after a given module lands
# (see the truth table in go.mod), and there is no atomic cross-repo merge.
# Pinning buys the window: cockpit keeps building against a known memql while
# that module lands, then ONE cockpit PR moves this pin and adds that module's
# require + replace in the same commit.
#
# TO BUMP: change the sha below, add the newly-landed module's `require` and
# `replace` to go.mod, and run `go mod tidy` -- all in one commit.
#
# Currently pinned to memql main after the app-session credential class
# landed (memql#4863) -- the identity node mints class="app_session" for a
# delegated run and the Library's byte routes admit that class as the user
# it names, which is what makes appsession.Library.Pull / .Push work at all.
# Before this the back-channel collapsed into class="service_account", a
# class that surface pins off deliberately, and every pull answered 401.
# memql-cockpit#371 is the cockpit half of that.
#
# WHAT THIS BUMP IS NOT. It does NOT carry the wire that epics memql#5096
# (tools on the ModelCall family, `message` control and `result` on app
# sessions, app descriptors on Register) and memql#5103 (ModelPullStart /
# Progress / End) own. Neither had merged when this moved. The cockpit
# halves of both are implemented against a narrow seam -- see
# internal/worker/appsession/session.go's controlPrompt and
# internal/worker/inference/pull.go -- so landing them is a pin bump plus
# the field mapping, not a rewrite. Do not read the presence of harness
# clients or the inference package as proof the wire exists.
#
# component/harness LOST its go.mod between the previous pin and this one,
# so its `require` and `replace` came OUT in the same commit. That is row 4
# of the truth table in go.mod read backwards: a replace with a require and
# no go.mod on the far side is "ambiguous import", and the fix is to delete
# both directives rather than to add anything. The remaining set is what
# `go mod tidy` converged on and is unchanged otherwise.
#
# ADVERTISEMENT STILL NEEDS NO PROTO CHANGE, which is worth knowing before
# reading the diff for one: models ride Register's EXISTING labels map as
# `model:<id>` and `runtime:<kind>`, per the engine's
# integrations/agent/worker/model_routing.go, and the params / quant / tools
# attributes this repository now advertises are more text inside that same
# map value. Only the SERVING half of tool calling depends on memql#5096.

